Let the given matrix be
\[A = \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix}\]
We want to find the determinant of $A$ as $x$ ranges over all real numbers.
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \begin{vmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} - 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cot^2 x \end{vmatrix} + 1 \begin{vmatrix} \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x \end{vmatrix} \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \frac{1}{\cos^2 x} \cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cot^2 x (1 - \cos^2 x) + \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x - 1) \\ &= \cot^2 x (\sin^2 x) + \cos^2 x (-\sin^2 x) \\ &= \cot^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x \\ &= \sin^2 x (\cot^2 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sin^2 x \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \cos^2 x \right) \\ &= \cos^2 x - \sin^2 x \cos^2 x \\ &= \cos^2 x (1 - \sin^2 x) \\ &= \cos^2 x (\cos^2 x) \\ &= \cos^4 x \end{align*}
So the determinant of the matrix is $\cos^4 x$.

Note: $\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x = \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} - \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} = \frac{\cos^2 x - 1}{\sin^2 x} = \frac{-\sin^2 x}{\sin^2 x} = -1$
Then
\begin{align*} \det(A) &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x \cos^2 x) - (\cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \csc^2 x) + (\cos^4 x - \cos^2 x) \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x (\cot^2 x - \csc^2 x)) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \sec^2 x (\cos^2 x (-1)) - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -\sec^2 x \cos^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x + \csc^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 - \cos^2 x \left( \frac{\cos^2 x}{\sin^2 x} \right) + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 - \frac{\cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \frac{1}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 + \frac{1 - \cos^4 x}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 + \frac{(1 - \cos^2 x)(1 + \cos^2 x)}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 + \frac{\sin^2 x (1 + \cos^2 x)}{\sin^2 x} + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 + (1 + \cos^2 x) + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= -1 + 1 + \cos^2 x + \cos^4 x - \cos^2 x \\ &= \cos^4 x \end{align*}

